From 43f56de28b9d3e56cc9d230c8f8d258ea55e20ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chimera Patch Builder <chimera@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 14:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] chimera: count and gate positive implicit-vector decisions

Replace the old cross-build census with one strict, function-level TSV
stream.  A decision is recorded only after legality and profitability choose
vector code.  Gated decisions are recorded as blocked and return before the
commit; ungated decisions are recorded as formed immediately before commit.

The late census id attribute lets SelectionDAG memop lowering retain the
post-inlining function identity without perturbing inlining decisions.
